sorry, i really don't like this. it's very hard for me to reason about this given the side effects on some other context. and then its nested in useObjectMenuContributions. 

I think something like this is much clearer and more testable. Fewer hooks; more imperative.

```ts
const Component = () => {
  const { setItems } = useMenuContext();
  useEffect(() => {
    setItem(items => createExtraItems());
  }, []);

  return <div>...</div>;
}
```

rather than

```ts
  useMagic();

  return <div>...</div>;
```

also i can't understand why there needs to be a registry.
this should be really simple.

it's like the other menu abstraction which has pretty much disabled me from being able to create menus -- i just can't figure it out by casual inspection and this kind of thing should be simple.

